Experiment 40: Automate Logout Functionality of a Web Application Using Selenium WebDriver

# AIM
To automate the logout functionality of a web application using Selenium WebDriver and verify that the user is successfully logged out.

# ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Import the required Selenium WebDriver packages.
3. Create an instance of ChromeDriver.
4. Open the web application login page.
5. Enter valid username and password.
6. Click the Login button.
7. Locate and click the Logout button.
8. Verify that the user is redirected to the login page.
9. Validate the logout result using JUnit assertions.
10. Close the browser.
11. Stop the program.

# CODE

**File: LogoutTest.java**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.By;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class LogoutTest {

    @Test
    public void testLogout() {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/login");

            driver.findElement(By.id("username"))
                  .sendKeys("tomsmith");

            driver.findElement(By.id("password"))
                  .sendKeys("SuperSecretPassword!");

            driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("button[type='submit']"))
                  .click();

            assertTrue(driver.getCurrentUrl().contains("/secure"));

            driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("a[href='/logout']"))
                  .click();

            assertTrue(driver.getCurrentUrl().contains("/login"));

            System.out.println("Logout completed successfully.");

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}
```

